524
00:25:59,394 --> 00:26:02,394
And so it was natural for us to do that.

525
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,394
And we had an enormous—we had

526
00:26:04,394 --> 00:26:06,394
close to a trillion dollars of assets

527
00:26:06,394 --> 00:26:07,394
to be invested in.

528
00:26:07,394 --> 00:26:08,394
Obviously.

529
00:26:08,394 --> 00:26:11,394
And so we had the funds and the

530
00:26:11,394 --> 00:26:14,394
capital that we needed to finance these new startups.

531
00:26:14,394 --> 00:26:16,394
And that was going quite well.

532
00:26:16,394 --> 00:26:19,894
One day, I had a call from Senator

533
00:26:19,894 --> 00:26:23,394
Ribicoff, who was a Connecticut senator at the time.

534
00:26:23,394 --> 00:26:27,394
And he wanted me to meet a young

535
00:26:27,394 --> 00:26:31,394
fellow who was running a financial services business.

536
